<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Menapii</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 53 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Belgic people of the Scheldt and lower Rhine who held off Caesar for years by retreating into their marshes and forests.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Menapii lived in the low, marshy lands of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/county-of-flanders">Flanders</a> and the southern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scheldt">Scheldt</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>. They joined the Belgic league in 57 BCE.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>They lived in scattered farmsteads and avoided pitched battle, withdrawing into woods and swamps. In 55 BCE the Germanic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/usipetes">Usipetes</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tencteri">Tencteri</a> crossed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> and seized part of their land.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Caesar campaigned against them in 56 and 55 BCE and finally subdued them in 53 BCE by burning their settlements. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> their capital was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cassel-nord">Castellum Menapiorum</a> (Cassel). The usurper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carausius">Carausius</a>, who ruled <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> from 286 CE, was a Menapian.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/menapii.jpg" alt="Menapii" width="320" height="240"><figcaption>Image: vzw Gallische Hoeve · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GallischeHoeve.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 53 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gaulish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Belgium, Netherlands</dd></dl></aside></div>

